    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T00:14:35Z",
    "body": "Escalated from effort:high to effort:max. Claim released.\n\nThe merge loops in recognize.rs combine coaxial walls without checking the axial gap.\nThe axial and radial pins return one 50 mm through hole across 34 mm of solid material.\nThe mouth pin also fails because the negative-side mouth is missing.\n\nHeld tests: mkinney:issue/2601-blind-radial-holes, commit ce2747ca1.\nRun: cargo test -p camcraft-motion --lib drilling::tests_opposite -- --nocapture\nAll three tests compile and fail on unchanged upstream/main 1ae4d061f.\nThe pins use a closed block with opposite D5 holes, each 8 mm deep, across a 50 mm span.\nThis reduced fixture does not cover the complete six-hole D50 bar.\n\nA span guard alone leaves the lower blind hole with the wrong entry and through status.\nHole has no direction field. CrossHole permits signed directions, but cross_drill rejects Z plunges.\nMill detection also excludes radial findings, and generation rejects mixed axial and radial lists.\nThe full fix needs a design for mouth direction and indexed hole dispatch.\nI chose to preserve the failing pins and raise the effort.\nI did not apply a partial span guard because it leaves incorrect hole records.\n\nNo production code changed. No PR opened. Mutation checks, the quick gate, and clippy were not run.\nNo goldens changed. The failing test names are:\n- opposite_blind_z_walls_keep_their_separate_depths\n- opposite_blind_radial_walls_keep_their_separate_depths\n- opposite_blind_radial_holes_enter_from_their_own_mouths\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
